{"explanation": "This unit responds to colored, tinted images whose subject fills a large part of the frame. Its activity is lowest on black-and-white or nearly colorless photos and higher whenever the photo has a noticeable warm or cool color cast. It is also more active when the main subject takes up a substantial part of the frame rather than being small, but the similar units share that size preference. The color-tint preference, especially the low response to colorless photos, is what sets this unit apart.", "rows": [18, 22, 23, 20]}
```

